+
+    // ==================== tiberius (STRATA_REGISTER_DAX): THE SLIDING WINDOW (default OFF) ====================
+    //
+    // Registers a WINDOW of the mapping with CUDA so the DEVICE can read the pack file's own pages, and slides
+    // that window as the prompt path walks the file.  The prompt path's direct-DMA branches already exist in both
+    // prefill paths and `pinned()`/`dma_ready()` are their only gate, so making the bytes DMA-able is the whole
+    // change: the 46.84 GiB expert file stops going through the stager's host copies.
+    //
+    // WHY A WINDOW AND NOT THE WHOLE MAPPING.  `cudaHostRegister` on the target machine caps the TOTAL registered
+    // host memory at ~7 GiB per process - measured, independent of free RAM (`ulimit -l` does not move it) - and
+    // the pack is 46.84 GiB, so a whole-mapping registration is refused.  What CAN be DMA-able is the part the
+    // reader is at: the pack is layer-contiguous, a layer is ~1 GiB, and the prompt path walks the layers in
+    // order, so a window of whole layers that keeps up with that walk makes every byte of the file directly
+    // DMA-able while never holding more than `STRATA_REGISTER_DAX_MIB` registered.  `prepare_layer` moves the
+    // window and carries the unregister-safety rule; the header describes the windows themselves.
+    //
+    // WHAT IT REQUIRES.  (1) A kernel whose fsdax GUP path accepts a LONGTERM pin - the `fsdax_longterm_pin=1`
+    // opt-in of the patched kernel; without it `cudaHostRegister` fails EINVAL, on this very mapping.  (2) A
+    // device with cudaDevAttrHostRegisterReadOnlySupported, which is why the call asks for
+    // cudaHostRegisterReadOnly.  (3) `cudaHostRegister` pins what is resident NOW and faults in what is not -
+    // which is the prefetch this design wants - so registering a window just before its layer is read is the
+    // cheap order.
+    //
+    // FAILURE IS GRACEFUL AND LOUD: a refused registration prints one line to stderr and the engine continues on
+    // the existing pageable path (`dma_ready()` then answers false and the prompt path builds its stager jobs
+    // exactly as it always did).  Registration is an optimization, never a prerequisite, so the flag is safe to
+    // set on a machine without the kernel opt-in - it just reports and does nothing.
+    //
+    // SIDE EFFECTS, all of them downstream of `dma_ready()` turning true: the prompt path stops staging through
+    // the copy threads (prefill.cpp); the verify window's PCIe groups may be formed from mapped experts as well
+    // as from the complement arena for whichever layers the window holds while a decode runs - the window is
+    // FROZEN during decode, because `begin_layer` is not a rotation point and rotating there would be 48
+    // register/unregister pairs a token; and the tuned share moves, because its conservative arm exists for host
+    // copies: `dma_ready()` in generate.cpp makes g_pinned_share 1.0, which takes the streamed ring from 96
+    // slots to 384 and the auto lend cap from 85% to 90% (`kAutoLendPct`).  Both stay overridable -
+    // STRATA_PREFILL_RING and STRATA_PREFILL_LEND_PCT still win - so A/B here is a config change, not a rebuild.
+    // `pin_cache_complement` additionally SKIPS its MADV_DONTNEED/POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED release loop for the
+    // layers the startup window holds: those pages are pinned for the device and cannot be dropped.
+    //
+    // THE RISK: a registered window is pinned while it is registered and nothing may truncate or hole-punch that
+    // file while the engine runs.  The window bounds what is charged to the process as unevictable at any one
+    // moment, and `close()` unregisters whatever is left before it unmaps.
+    const char* register_dax = std::getenv("STRATA_REGISTER_DAX");
+    if (register_dax != nullptr && register_dax[0] != '\0' && std::strcmp(register_dax, "0") != 0) {
+        // The budget bounds the WINDOW, not a prefix of the file.  0 / unset = the driver's own ~7 GiB cap.
+        const char* mib = std::getenv("STRATA_REGISTER_DAX_MIB");
+        const long long mib_value = mib != nullptr ? std::atoll(mib) : 0;
+        dax_budget_ = mib_value > 0 ? (uint64_t) mib_value << 20 : (6144ull << 20);
+        std::fprintf(stderr,
+                     "FileExpertSource: STRATA_REGISTER_DAX: sliding window of %.2f GiB over a %.2f GiB pack "
+                     "(%lld layers, %.2f GiB per layer)\n",
+                     (double) dax_budget_ / 1073741824.0, (double) mapped_bytes_ / 1073741824.0,
+                     (long long) n_layers_, (double) mapped_bytes_ / 1073741824.0 / (double) n_layers_);
+        // Open on the first run of layers that fits, so the first chunk of a prompt pays no rotation to start.
+        if (n_layers_ > 0 && !layer_blob_bytes_.empty() && layer_end(0) <= dax_budget_ && dax_register_run(0))
+            dax_ok_ = true;
+        if (dax_ok_) {
+            std::fprintf(stderr,
+                         "FileExpertSource: STRATA_REGISTER_DAX: window on layers %lld..%lld, %.2f GiB "
+                         "registered%s; the prompt path DMAs straight out of it\n",
+                         (long long) dax_windows_.front().first, (long long) dax_windows_.front().last,
+                         (double) dax_windows_.front().bytes / 1073741824.0,
+                         dax_windows_.front().device != nullptr ? " (device alias ok)" : " (NO device alias)");
+        } else {
