+/// `cudaHostRegister` takes PAGE-ALIGNED addresses only, and a layer's byte span is the pack's own arithmetic
+/// (`512 x blob_bytes`) rather than a multiple of the page size, so every window bound is rounded outwards.  The
+/// rounding can make two adjacent windows share a page, which is why a registration evicts anything it overlaps.
+uint64_t host_page_size() {
